-- title:
--   Dimensions of a p-divisible group and its Cartier dual sum to the height
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, assumed Noetherian and complete for the maximal-ideal-adic topology, let $p$ be a prime and $h$ a natural number, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$. Let $G$ and $G'$ be $p$-divisible groups of height $h$ over $R$ in the sense of the project structure: each carries levels $G.\mathrm{level}(v)$, commutative cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebras that are finite free of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra–algebra maps $G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to G.\mathrm{level}(v)$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity. Let $D$ be a Cartier duality between them, i.e. isomorphisms $G'.\mathrm{level}(v)\cong \mathrm{CartierDual}_R(G.\mathrm{level}(v))$ compatible with the transition maps of $G'$ and with multiplication by $p$ on $G$. Suppose $G$ has dimension $n$ and $G'$ has dimension $n'$, meaning that for every $v$ the cotangent module $I_v/I_v^2$ of the augmentation ideal of the $v$-th level is isomorphic, as an $R$-module, to $(R/p^vR)^n$, respectively $(R/p^vR)^{n'}$. Then $n+n'=h$.
--
--   This is Tate's relation $\dim G+\dim G'=\operatorname{ht} G$ for a $p$-divisible group and its Cartier dual over a local base of residue characteristic $p$. It is used in the construction, for a $p$-divisible group over a ring of integers, of a basis of the Tate module after passage to $\mathbf{C}_p$ on which the Galois action is given by powers of the cyclotomic character.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_add_eq_height_of_hasDimension_of_cartierDuality.lean

